"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 12 and pathological findings demonstrating pT3b disease with positive surgical margins and seminal vesicle invasion. The Gleason score was 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3). These are significant adverse features. Countervailing findings include the absence of documented lymph node metastasis and no reported lymphovascular invasion. Missing information regarding subsequent postoperative PSA trajectory would significantly impact risk stratification. Further data on the PSA level following surgery is crucial for refining this prognosis. The current assessment relies heavily on the pathological staging derived from the prostatectomy specimen, as biopsy-to-prostatectomy differences are noted due to missing Gleason pattern and ISUP report from the initial biopsy. The fixed estimated horizon is 38.08 months. This is a predicted recurrence horizon, not evidence of observed recurrence. The sensitivity range is 30.47–45.70 months; its coverage has not been validated."
